    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics is my passion, especially algebra and geometry. I find it intuitive and creative, like solving puzzles. As a student in upper secondary, I enjoy applying it to real-world problems, such as calculating sports stats from football. It’s challenging but rewarding, and I love how it connects to art and logic.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I don’t usually get anxious about math. My parents’ strong educational backgrounds helped me build confidence early on. I’m a high extraversion and conscientiousness person, so I approach problems step by step. If I’m stuck, I take breaks or talk to peers, which keeps me calm and focused.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used AI tools like ChatGPT to check my algebra homework. It was helpful for explaining steps clearly and catching mistakes. I felt more confident because it didn’t judge me—just gave straightforward, friendly guidance. It’s a great supplement for my learning.",
