    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math learning by adapting to individual needs, like explaining concepts in simple terms or generating practice problems. They can also provide instant feedback on homework, helping students identify mistakes early. This makes learning more engaging and less intimidating, especially for those who struggle with traditional methods."
